      "id": "policy",
      "type": "inputNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 420,
        "y": 80
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "Activation Assessment Contract",
        "nodeType": "text_input",
        "properties": {
          "message": "Evaluate activation levels for the supplied operations using the supplied context. Each operation has an identifier, description, current activation level, activation threshold, and recorded activity. Timestamps identify when records were produced; intentions and requested work are distinct from recorded results. Return updates containing operationId, activation, reason, and instruction. activation is an absolute level from 0 to 100. Each update replaces that operation’s previous level. In Semi Auto, each returned update at 100 requests its operation through the Work Coordinator. In Full Auto, the returned update with the highest activation requests its operation regardless of whether it has reached 100. If updates share the highest activation, their returned order determines which is selected. An omitted operation retains its recorded level and is not newly requested. reason records the basis for the update; instruction supplies context to the selected operation. Updates may raise, lower, or retain levels, and the updates list may be empty.",
          "inputKey": ""
        }
      }
